meta {
  name: SetCredential
  type: grpc
  seq: 2
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.ResourceService/SetCredential
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "resource_id": "res-github",
      "secret": "Z2hwX2V4ZW1wbG8tZGUtdG9rZW4="
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0017, convention 5). The `ctx` field the messages still declare is ignored
  by the server — do not use it: it gives the false impression of scoping the
  call.

  The secret goes to the `SecretStore` — locally, a Kubernetes Secret (there is no
  emulator of GCP Secret Manager). The response carries only the `credential_ref`.

  In an organization account, prefer an ORGANIZATION credential (a GitHub App): a
  personal token dies when the person leaves (ADR-0003).
}
